[36m(TaskRunner pid=67616)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=67616)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form. Since \(|z| = 4\), we can write \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=67616)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=67616)[0m Substituting \(z = 4e^{i\theta}\) into the expression, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=67616)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=67616)[0m (75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=67616)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=67616)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=67616)[0m First, let's simplify the expression:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=67616)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=67616)[0m (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) = 4(75\cos\theta + 75i\sin\theta + 117i\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) = 4((75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta))
[36m(TaskRunner pid=67616)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=67616)[0m \[
